(polyline (pts (xy 408.00 128.00) (xy 408.00 200.00)) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid) (color 32 96 176 1)) (uuid "107b7898-983e-4efb-8516-4525304542cd"))
(polyline (pts (xy 408.00 200.00) (xy 204.00 200.00)) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid) (color 32 96 176 1)) (uuid "ee037b25-ea21-4d37-8ae0-942765b467a7"))
(polyline (pts (xy 204.00 200.00) (xy 204.00 128.00)) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid) (color 32 96 176 1)) (uuid "ea8cc92b-ed50-430a-bcd8-97ee9067fbfe"))
(text "4  -  HALF-BRIDGE GATE DRIVERS   (IRS2104, 520 ns dead-time)" (at 207.0 133.4 0) (effects (font (size 2.3 2.3) (bold yes) (color 32 96 176 1)) (justify left)) (uuid "4a14ba3b-0c50-463e-bee9-25c5d31f5b64"))
(polyline (pts (xy 204.00 206.00) (xy 408.00 206.00)) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid) (color 32 96 176 1)) (uuid "23d9c561-f638-4cea-8baa-9bea1307871e"))
(polyline (pts (xy 408.00 206.00) (xy 408.00 268.00)) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid) (color 32 96 176 1)) (uuid "9edcadea-288e-4002-942a-e5c6551030a0"))
(polyline (pts (xy 408.00 268.00) (xy 204.00 268.00)) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid) (color 32 96 176 1)) (uuid "2af69e14-05ad-444c-8692-92b1e0cc9712"))
(polyline (pts (xy 204.00 268.00) (xy 204.00 206.00)) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid) (color 32 96 176 1)) (uuid "c0d5704d-728c-49ba-8e6b-133ca5ff3e1a"))
(text "5  -  HARDWARE OVER-CURRENT TRIP + LATCH   (firmware-independent)" (at 207.0 211.4 0) (effects (font (size 2.3 2.3) (bold yes) (color 32 96 176 1)) (justify left)) (uuid "5a086747-6bc2-478a-84fd-b47cea56e511"))
(text_box "Fed from +12 V, not from VBUS: on a legacy port VBUS sits at ~4.75 V at the connector, below the LP2950 dropout for a 5 V output.  Rails therefore come up identically on either port type." (at 124 240 0) (size 68 18) (margins 0.9 0.9 0.9 0.9) (stroke (width 0) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05) ) (justify left top)) (uuid "7ea1c067-794c-41d3-be10-cff02200d5b3"))
(text_box "Why an on-board boost: the IRS2104 needs 10-12 V of gate drive (UVLO 8.9 V typ) to put the bridge FETs at their rated RDS(on).  This 10 uH / SS34 stage makes 12 V at 150 mA from any contract between 5 V and 20 V, so the drivers behave the same on a legacy 5 V port as on a 20 V one." (at 16 234 0) (size 94 22) (margins 0.9 0.9 0.9 0.9) (stroke (width 0) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05) ) (justify left top)) (uuid "92f1eb6a-1fb4-4d35-b2b9-f5d47d06c74c"))
(text_box "ISNS sits on the inverting input, so an over-current drives the open-collector output LOW and pulls SHDN_N down within ~1 us with no firmware involved.  Both IRS2104 SD pins hang on SHDN_N, as does the MCU (open-drain), giving a wired-AND kill." (at 206 252 0) (size 83.3 18.823529411764707) (margins 0.9 0.9 0.9 0.9) (stroke (width 0) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0) ) (justify left top)) (uuid "66c386d3-3cad-4917-80ca-262f9cd46a77"))
(text_box "The 4R7 + 2n2 snubbers damp the switch-node ringing set by FET Coss and layout inductance.  60 V FETs, because a 20 V contract plus that ringing will exceed a 30 V part." (at 298 112 0) (size 92 14) (margins 0.9 0.9 0.9 0.9) (stroke (width 0) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0) ) (justify left top)) (uuid "de20bbdd-8b78-4f4c-bc63-9a11e003ea0d"))
(text_box "PD contract: CFG1/2/3 select 5 / 9 / 12 / 15 / 20 V.  CFG1 is pulled high so a bare board requests 5 V before firmware runs.  500 ms after plug-in the MCU re-reads ADC_VBUS; no rise means a legacy 5 V port and the firmware clamps the output range instead of faulting.  The PDO is re-selected as the setpoint changes (table on the title page), with the output disabled during renegotiation." (at 16 116 0) (size 168 20) (margins 0.9 0.9 0.9 0.9) (stroke (width 0) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05) ) (justify left top)) (uuid "f068b83a-adcd-4ae2-8656-1c70da577201"))
(text_box "Each bootstrap capacitor returns to its own VS pin, which is tied to the switch node it references - that is what lets the cap refresh and the high-side FET turn on.  10R gate resistors slow the edges enough to keep the ringing in hand." (at 206 186 0) (size 86 16) (margins 0.9 0.9 0.9 0.9) (stroke (width 0) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 0.95 0.95) ) (justify left top)) (uuid "ba6ef38c-4262-4fbb-9d8a-2f11a3c59d70"))
